// RUN: timeout 1 %clang @%S/Inputs/slow.argsfile %s -o %t-ogcg.o
// RUN: timeout 1 %clang @%S/Inputs/slow.argsfile %s -fclangir -fclangir-mem2reg -o %t-cir.o
// XFAIL: *

// This is a preprocessed 220K-line translation unit from a real codebase, with
// its own identifiers renamed. It targets aarch64-none-linux-android24 with -Os and gnu++20. The file is
// dominated by heavy template usage (~9,600 template declarations), Eigen
// linear algebra expression templates (~3,870 Eigen references across 185
// headers), ~7,100 inline functions, ~5,950 constexpr items, and ~3,650
// operator overloads. It includes a polymorphic model factory with ~20+
// model types, each templated on float/double.
//
// OGCG timing (measured on a build machine):
//   Wall clock:    ~65 seconds
//   Max RSS:       ~3.3 GB
//   IPC:           1.63
//   Cache misses:  15.7%
//   -ftime-report: Frontend 20s (26%), LLVM IR gen 13s (17%),
//                  Optimizer 32s (41%), MachineCodeGen 13s (16%)
//
// ClangIR timing:
//   Does not complete within 120s; estimated ~50 MINUTES total (~50x slower).
//   Within 120s of execution:
//     Instructions:  893B (vs OGCG's 312B in 66s — ~70x more total work)
//     IPC:           2.55 (not memory-bound, just doing far more computation)
//     Cache misses:  12.8%
//
// Perf profile comparison (30s snapshot — biased toward shared frontend):
//   CIR-specific hotspots NOT present in OGCG:
//     - ParametricStorageUniquer::DenseSetImpl::insert_as()  1.52%
//     - mlir::detail::AttributeUniquer::getWithTypeID<StringAttr>()  0.54%
//   Functions amplified in CIR vs OGCG:
//     - RecordDecl::field_begin():  2.64% vs 1.66% (+59%)
//     - __memcmp_evex_movbe:        2.38% vs 1.31% (+82%)
//
// The bottleneck is NOT memory latency (IPC is higher for CIR). The CIR
// pipeline simply executes ~70x more instructions than OGCG. The LLVM IR
// generation phase that CIR replaces (AST->LLVM IR, 13s in OGCG) becomes
// AST->CIR + CIR lowering->LLVM IR, consuming an estimated ~2,900+ seconds.
// This suggests algorithmic issues in CIR emission and/or lowering, not just
// constant-factor overhead.
//
// We need to identify and fix all performance regressions to get this within
// 1.5x of OGCG's time (~90 seconds).

